{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed1425705205/1/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1425705205/1`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed1425705205/1/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n- `description`：识别网格中由 grey 连线配对的形状对，将每对中较大形状沿连线暗示的轴线折叠，使其与较小形状重合，并用较小形状的颜色覆盖重叠区域。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景色为 black。网格中散布着若干彩色形状，每个形状是一个由单一颜色像素组成的 4-连通区域。\n  - 形状成对出现：每对中两个形状颜色不同，但其中较小的形状在几何上是较大形状沿某条对称轴（水平或垂直）翻折后能完全覆盖的一个子区域的形状。换言之，较大形状可以沿某条轴线折叠，折叠后的一半恰好与较小形状全等。\n  - 每对形状之间通过一条由 grey 像素组成的单像素细线段相连（水平或垂直），这条线段同时也暗示了折叠轴的方向（与连线垂直的方向为折叠轴方向）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 通过 grey 连线识别形状配对关系。\n  - 对每一对，确定折叠轴方向：若连线为水平线段，则折叠轴为垂直方向；若连线为垂直线段，则折叠轴为水平方向。\n  - 将较大形状沿其自身中线（与折叠轴方向一致的中心线）折叠，即将远离较小形状的那一半翻转叠到靠近较小形状的一半上。折叠后较大形状在输出中缩小为原来的一半。\n  - 将较小形状平移到与折叠后的较大形状完全重合的位置。重叠处像素变为较小形状的颜色，非重叠处保留较大形状的颜色。\n  - grey 连线在输出中被移除。\n- `Key insight`：grey 连线不仅标识配对关系，还隐含地编码了折叠轴的方向（与连线垂直）。解题者需要发现这一几何对偶关系，并理解\"较大形状折叠后与较小形状全等\"这一空间约束，才能正确完成变换。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/89565ca0, train/3bd292e8, train/11dc524f, train/9f669b64, train/465b7d93, train/84ba50d3, train/337b420f, eval/7b80bb43\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"89565ca0\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3682\nmechanism=0.4869\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:closed_region, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/89565ca0.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/89565ca0.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConvert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.\n- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.\n- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.\n\nRule:\n- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.\n- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.\n- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.\n- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.\n\nKey insight:\n- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"colored partitioned frame line drawings; ignore scattered pad-color pixels\",\n  \"dst\": \"stack one horizontal bar per frame, ordered by count of enclosed background regions then color id\",\n  \"transform\": \"bar length = number of enclosed 4-connected background regions; pad right with the scattered color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height = number of frame colors, width = maximum enclosed-region count\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3bd292e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3346\nmechanism=0.3700\nlexical=0.0151\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:line_segment, operation:draw_line, operation:reflect, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3bd292e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3bd292e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor wall-separated background regions alternately, starting with grey in the lower-left region.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground wall color.\n- The wall pixels form one or more 4-connected one-cell-thick segments.\n- Each wall segment separates exactly two 4-connected background regions.\nRule\n- Keep all wall pixels unchanged.\n- Label the 4-connected background regions and connect two labels when they\n  touch opposite sides of the same wall segment.\n- Color the region containing the lower-left corner grey, then flip between\n  grey and green across every wall adjacency.\nKey insight\n- The red walls define a bipartite map of regions; the lower-left background\n  region fixes which side of the alternating coloring is grey.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected orange background regions separated by red one-cell-thick wall segments\",\n  \"transform\": \"keep red wall pixels; recolor the lower-left background region grey and recolor each wall-adjacent region with the opposite grey/green color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"11dc524f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3465\nmechanism=0.4176\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:reflect, operation:translate, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/11dc524f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/11dc524f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide the non-square sprite to the square anchor and replace the anchor with the sprite's mirror image.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- There is one 8-connected non-background sprite that is not a solid 2x2 square.\n- There is one solid 2x2 square anchor in another non-background color.\n\nRule:\n- Move the sprite straight toward the anchor along their unique cardinal separation until it touches the anchor's near edge.\n- Reflect the moved sprite across that near edge and draw the reflected copy in the anchor color.\n- Clear the original locations; the output keeps only the moved sprite and reflected anchor-color copy.\n\nKey insight:\n- The 2x2 square marks the mirror line: its side facing the sprite becomes the contact edge for a two-color reflected pair.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"8-connected non-square foreground sprite s\",\n  \"dst\": \"solid 2x2 square anchor d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s faces d by cardinal separation with overlapping span\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s to touch d's facing edge, mirror s across that edge in d.color, and clear originals\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f669b64\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3432\nmechanism=0.4130\nlexical=0.0119\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f669b64.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9f669b64.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\n  horizontal or vertical axis.\n- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\n- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\n  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\n\nRule\n- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\n  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\n- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\n- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\n  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\n- Keep the other end object unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\n  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"middle solid rectangular object between two end objects\",\n  \"path\": \"straight horizontal or vertical line away from the non-target end object and through the perpendicular solid target rectangle/bar\",\n  \"dst\": \"place flush with the grid edge beyond the target\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint only the final moved rectangle at dst\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase original source pixels; split the target rectangle/bar along the moving object's two-cell-wide path and shift its two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement; keep the other end object unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"465b7d93\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3646\nmechanism=0.4569\nlexical=0.0121\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:translate, relation:between, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular\n  one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.\n- The frame interior is initially background.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the original sprite from its outside location.\n- Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to\n  interior extremes.\n- Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of\n  adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside\n  those drawn segments.\n\nKey insight:\nThe outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,\nnot a bitmap to scale by block replication.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"small colored sprite s outside the frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"hollow rectangular frame interior d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"unique s maps to unique d; s.bbox extremes align to d.bbox extremes\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; stretch s into d by mapping bbox extremes, drawing 4-adjacent segments, and filling enclosed regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"84ba50d3\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3569\nmechanism=0.4624\nlexical=0.0123\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/84ba50d3.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/84ba50d3.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the blue sprites downward relative to the red divider, with vertical sprites passing through to the bottom.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One non-background color forms a single full-width horizontal divider row.\n- The other non-background color forms 4-connected sprites above the divider.\n\nRule:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
